  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "SharpVision.Terminal 1.6.0-beta.2 prerelease: version-aligned with the other SharpVision packages; no functional changes since 1.6.0-beta.1, which added job control (SIGTSTP suspend with terminal restore, SIGCONT re-enter and repaint), negotiates DEC private mode 2027 for grapheme-cluster width, and adds a raw-escape binding tier for non-ECMA-48 keys. Protocol and host fixes cover eager-wrap terminals (bottom-right cell skip, scroll-reuse disable, xenl for Windows VT), terminal-title push and restore as one atomic leased step, DA1 written last so its reply fences every earlier probe, direct-color program synthesis so true color reaches the wire, color depth treated as an evidence lattice, xterm-compatible recognition beyond the \"xterm\" substring, architecture-specific TIOCGWINSZ/ISIG/termios layout, SUSP disabled so Ctrl+Z cannot suspend raw mode, flat lone-Escape latency, stalled-paste recovery with literal routed payloads preserved, Kitty functional keys and legacy mouse reports preserved, PaneVisible driven by live outer-terminal focus events, and a UTF-8-aware Windows console host that reads on a pooled thread and flushes its input buffer on restore. See https://github.com/pavkam/sharp-vision/blob/main/docs/protocols/coverage-matrix.md for the implemented protocol surface and fallback behavior.",
